  "result": "Perfect! Credit notes are complete. All 232 tests pass.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error** to src/errors.js for when credit note amount exceeds invoice total\n\n2. **New src/credits.js** with:\n   - Helper function `nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, date)` that:\n     - Filters existingNumbers to only CN (credit note) numbers for the given year\n     - Generates sequential numbers: CN-YYYY-COUNTER format\n     - Independently counts credit notes (separate from invoice counters)\n     - Zero-pads counter to 4 digits\n   \n   - Main function `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` that:\n     - Validates invoice status is NOT 'draft' (NOT_ISSUED error for drafts)\n     - Works with 'issued', 'partially_paid', and 'paid' invoices\n     - Validates date is valid (DATE_INVALID error)\n     - Validates amount is positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n     - Validates amount \u2264 invoice total (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error)\n     - Returns ok(creditNote) with: `{ number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }`\n\n3. **20 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Creating credit notes for all valid invoice statuses (issued, partially_paid, paid)\n   - Error handling: NOT_ISSUED, DATE_INVALID, AMOUNT_INVALID variants, CREDIT_TOO_HIGH\n   - Amount validation (zero, negative, non-integer, exceeding total)\n   - Sequential numbering with year reset\n   - Separate counter from invoices\n   - Zero-padding and formatting\n   - Invoices with discounts, vouchers, and complex line items\n   - VAT calculations\n\nCredit notes enable refunds on issued invoices with proper tracking and sequential numbering.",
